<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - CCU starts.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - CCU starts.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- ING Barings analyst Marla Marron said she had started coverage of Chilean brewer Compaa Cerveceras Unidas with a rating of hold.</p>
<p>-- In a February 6 report, she wrote that beer volumes probably would remain lackluster, but volumes in Argentina should rebound by an estimated five to six percent in 1997.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Nevertheless, we do not expect CCU's Argentine operation to turn profitable until 1998.&quot;</p>
<p>-- She set a price target of $18.50. The company's American Depositary Receipts were trading up 13/64 at 16-7/8.</p>
<p>((-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
